# DNA Pattern Recognition

## Problem Summary

Write a query to identify specific patterns in each DNA sequence, including whether it starts with ATG, ends with a stop codon (TAA, TAG, or TGA), and contains the patterns ATAT and GGG.

## Solution

```sql
select sample_id, dna_sequence, species, 
case
    when left(dna_sequence, 3) = 'ATG' then 1
    else 0
end as has_start,
case
    when right(dna_sequence, 3) IN ('TAA', 'TAG', 'TGA') then 1
    else 0
end as has_stop,
case
    WHEN dna_sequence LIKE '%ATAT%' THEN 1
    else 0
end as has_atat,
case
    WHEN dna_sequence LIKE '%GGG%' THEN 1
    else 0
end as has_ggg
from samples;
```
